WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.200
Lab 1 needs PowerShell and Python
on a laptop, and nothing else.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.202
First, run Microsoft's
rule over the fixture:

3
00:00:07.202 --> 00:00:11.038
of four credentials added on
the second day, it finds one.

4
00:00:11.038 --> 00:00:15.287
Then confirm the run needs four read
permissions and nothing that writes.

5
00:00:15.287 --> 00:00:17.531
Run the first day with no baseline,

6
00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:20.737
and it writes a baseline
candidate with its hash.

7
00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:25.438
In real life a second person reviews
that candidate and passes you the hash.

8
00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:28.847
Then run the second day
against the approved baseline,

9
00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:33.070
and the drift appears: more findings
and more warnings than day one.
